20. In view of the above, the legal issues involved herein, can be summarised as under:-
(i) An application under Order IX Rule 13 CPC cannot be filed by a person who was not initially a party to the proceedings;
(ii) Inherent powers under Section 151 CPC can be exercised by the Court to redress only such a grievance, for which no remedy is provided for under the CPC;
(iii) In the event that an order has been obtained from the Court by playing fraud upon it, it is always open to the Court to recall the said order on the application of the person aggrieved, and such power can also be NEUTRAL CITATION C/SCA/26641/2022 ORDER DATED: 17/01/2024 undefined exercised by the appellate court;
(iv) Where the fraud has been committed upon a party, the court cannot investigate such a factual issue, and in such an eventuality, a party has the right to get the said judgment or order set aside, by filing an independent suit.
Achyut Chinubhai vs Special Land Acquisition Officer on 17 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/174197319/
4 (v) A person aggrieved may maintain an application before the Land Acquisition Collector for reference under Section 18 or 30 of the Act, 1894, but cannot make an application for impleadment or apportionment before the Reference Court."
